<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>☁️ LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT OBSERVATION + MODEL FILL (GOES FD 10-min + RRFS/GDPS fallback)</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA GOES-East (GOES-19) + GOES-West (GOES-18) ABI L2 Clear Sky Mask full-disk observations, RRFS TCDC fallback, GDPS fallback<br/><a href="https://www.goes.noaa.gov/">https://www.goes.noaa.gov/</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p><p><b>Coverage</b> — one at a time, switched right here in this folder:<br>◉ <b>Global Coverage</b> (shown)<br>○ North America Coverage<br>○ Great Lakes Basin Coverage<br>Pro switches exclusively. Web/app: check exactly one box.</p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Coverage:</b> Global Coverage<br><b>Precedence:</b> 1) Valid GOES-East/GOES-West full-disk BCM (DQF==0). 2) RRFS TCDC where GOES invalid/missing. 3) GDPS TotalCloudCover only for verified remaining gaps. Missing satellite pixels are NEVER rendered as clear sky.<br><b>Provenance:</b> {'GOES-19': '2026-10-14 19:30Z valid-cells=3904271/g=2342887', 'GOES-18': '2026-10-14 19:30Z valid-cells=3435476/g=2343135', 'RRFS-TCDC': 'rrfs.20261014 n=2632946/g=1195390', 'GDPS-TCC': 'GDPS_15km_TotalCloudCover n=5273396/g=6479996'}</p><p><b>Coverage</b> — one at a time, switched right here in this folder:<br>◉ <b>Global Coverage</b> (shown)<br>○ North America Coverage<br>○ Great Lakes Basin Coverage<br>Pro switches exclusively. Web/app: check exactly one box.</p>]]></description>
      <Style>
        <ListStyle>
          <listItemType>radioFolder</listItemType>
        </ListStyle>
      </Style>
